ormat="epo"><addressbook><name>ICHIKAWA SATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOKYO SHIBAURA ELECTRIC CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ICHIKAWA, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KABUSHIKI KAISHA TOSHIBA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ICHIKAWA SATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ICHIKAWA, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A band filter whose bandwidth and cutoff characteristic are freely set without requiring sophisticated design or adjustments. To provide such a filter, a surface acoustic wave device is composed of a main filter (Fm) and a subfilter (Fs) that are connected in parallel. The subfilter (Fs) has a frequency-attenuation characteristic that includes a stop band in the frequency range corresponding to the passband of the main filter (Fm), and the frequency-attenuation characteristic of the subfilter (Fs) includes a transition to its passband in the slope outside passband of the main filter (Fm), with the result that the phases of signals are opposite.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un filtre de bande dont la largeur de bande et la caractéristique de coupure sont librement fixées sans nécessiter une conception ou des réglages complexes. Un tel filtre est fourni par un dispositif d'onde acoustique de surface constitué d'un filtre principal (Fm) et d'un sous filtre (Fs) reliés en parallèle. Le sous filtre (Fs) présente une caractéristique d'atténuation de fréquence comprenant une bande d'arrêt dans la gamme de fréquence correspondant à la bande passante du filtre principale (Fm), ainsi qu'une transition vers sa bande passante dans la pente à l'extérieur du filtre principal (Fm), le résultat étant que les phases de signaux sont opposées.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>